# openHC — EA family EXTERNAL toolchain selection.
#
# NOT part of the normal defconfig composition. build/build.sh appends this file
# (plus a generated BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_PATH line) ONLY when OHC_EA_SDK points
# at a pre-built EA toolchain — see build.sh and .github/workflows/images.yml.
# Without OHC_EA_SDK the EA boards build their own internal glibc toolchain from
# board/ea/common/common_defconfig exactly as before; this file is never read.
#
# Why: all five EA boards are the SAME target (x86_64 Bonnell, glibc, C++/wchar),
# so the ~15-min host-gcc is identical. CI builds it ONCE in a `toolchain` job,
# packages output/host, and the five image jobs consume it here as an external
# toolchain instead of each rebuilding it from cold.
#
# These lines appear AFTER the family common_defconfig in the composition, so the
# BR2_TOOLCHAIN choice flips from the internal glibc toolchain to this external
# one (kconfig takes the last assignment of a choice). The capability flags below
# MUST match what the SDK actually is or Buildroot's toolchain check fails loudly
# at configure time — EXCEPT BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CXX, which if omitted silently
# drops every C++ package (ICU, harfbuzz, WPE WebKit), so it is the one to never miss.
#
# Must track board/ea/common/common_defconfig + board/common/common_defconfig:
#   GCC_14      <- Buildroot 2026.02.3 default gcc for x86_64 (14.3.0)
#   HEADERS_6_19 <- board/common sets BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_LINUX_HEADERS_CUSTOM_6_19
#   CUSTOM_GLIBC <- the family runs glibc (PowerVR DDK blobs are glibc-linked)
#   CXX          <- C++/wchar for WPE WebKit + ICU
# For a glibc external toolchain Buildroot assumes wchar/locale/threads/NPTL/SSP/RPC,
# so those are not (and cannot be) set here.
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CUSTOM=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_PREINSTALLED=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CUSTOM_PREFIX="x86_64-buildroot-linux-gnu"
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_GCC_14=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_HEADERS_6_19=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CUSTOM_GLIBC=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_CXX=y
# BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_PATH is appended by build.sh from $OHC_EA_SDK.
